	(text "Through-hole level shifters. There is no DIP version of the 74ALVC164245, so each direction is its own chip."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.89 25.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "020b3192-3561-40ed-bab1-eb2ad4c465ed")
	)
	(text "U17  NOR: MWRT = not pWR* and not sOUT. JP1 is a pin header; fit the jumper only with no front panel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 270.32 521.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0240adb3-23b8-4bce-a37c-086047ad5e20")
	)
	(text "U15 unused inverters, inputs grounded"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.32 475.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "152ba697-2880-4429-a4b2-d3b81586eb32")
	)
	(text "74ACT245, supply 5 V: the FPGA side is the input (3.3 V is a valid high) and the S-100 side is the 5 V output. Direction is strapped A to B, pin 1 to 5 V. 74LVC245, supply 3.3 V: the S-100 side is the input (these inputs accept 5 V) and the FPGA side is the 3.3 V output. Direction is strapped B to A, pin 1 to 0 V. Pin 19, marked CE on the symbol, is the active-low output enable. LS_BUS_DIR and LS_DATA_DIR stay on the FPGA connector with pull-ups, and are not wired to a direction pin: reversing a 74ACT245 would drive 5 V into the FPGA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.89 31.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "176552fa-1e78-46d1-b31b-3ce1bbc1daae")
	)
	(text "U9  strobes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 464.89 49.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "20ba8a99-9565-4127-a098-2f97556cc3e6")
	)
	(text "U7  A16-A23"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.89 49.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2b327e01-c57d-445e-bc3f-b4764c5528ff")
	)
	(text "Each FPGA input has 10 k to 3.3 V inside a bussed resistor network, so every output stays off while the FPGA is still configuring. The buffer, not the FPGA pin, sinks the terminator current. The bus side has no pull-up of its own: the backplane terminator holds these lines at 2.7 V through 270 ohm. Pin 98 ERROR* and pin 99 POC* are not on that terminator, so only those two have 2.2 k to 5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.05 234.35 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "48aca9a0-a680-48ba-bb87-6ccdbaaa8af7")
	)
	(text "J5: 16-way cable to the IMSAI CP-A front panel. 1 k pull-ups to 5 V, as on the MPU-A. The panel pulls lines low with open-collector drivers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.32 591.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "666f39ae-e772-4523-a9f9-9a9d55a868bf")
	)
	(text "U10  PHI, pHLDA, PWAIT, CLOCK, PINTE (always enabled)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.89 137.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "699bf850-5cb9-44c4-99c5-4695c3272eea")
	)
	(text "U13  data in, from DI0-DI7"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 357.89 137.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "728ae105-2799-4e90-ae29-e170cb8910d7")
	)
	(text "U15 inverts SSW_DSB*. U16: while the front panel pulls SSW_DSB* low, U14 turns on and U13 and U12 turn off, so the panel byte reaches the FPGA and is copied out to DO. U12 also stays off until the FPGA enables the bus. U17 plus JP1 make MWRT for a chassis with no front panel. Leave JP1 open in an IMSAI: the CP-A drives MWRITE."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.32 465.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "73de501f-e098-487f-9bda-1f3785f02429")
	)
	(text "U10 input pull-downs. While the FPGA is unconfigured these lines sit low, so the bus clocks stay low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.89 197.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "79ef8e51-8037-4a26-a67d-c9e5709206fc")
	)
	(text "Decoupling: one 100 nF disc at the supply pin of every IC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.32 573.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7f1a17f2-2e88-4823-af6f-fa20a20ca18d")
	)
	(text "U5  A0-A7"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.89 49.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8fa39eeb-35a3-4db9-b1c0-15315a96289b")
	)
	(text "U8  status"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 357.89 49.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "94c9278a-f0b8-4850-b59d-ef908a662e84")
	)
	(text "U12  FPGA to front-panel cable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 250.89 137.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a4e8135c-44b7-4235-929d-42d6e039bf6a")
	)
	(text "Check the pin order against your cable before ordering boards. Assumed here: odd pins D0 to D7, even pins ground."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.32 595.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a6ccee84-ff66-40ba-a894-5f93861aed19")
	)
	(text "U14  front-panel cable to FPGA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 464.89 137.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a95ac10a-6042-4d81-86c8-9f6ef5275078")
	)
	(text "Every output enable is pulled up, so the transceivers stay off until the FPGA is configured. Exception: U10 is enabled all the time, and its inputs are pulled down so PHI and CLOCK stay low until then."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.89 37.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ce67246e-c829-49df-8e15-7d4b7f475cf0")
	)
	(text "U16  OR. Gate 1 disables DI while the panel drives. Gate 2 disables the cable driver until the FPGA enables the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.32 521.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ce6dff08-6cd1-42a9-a976-f2bb25809647")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups so the output enables stay off, and the two unused direction pins sit high, until the FPGA drives them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.32 573.81 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f4e09dd2-6d23-47e4-afe0-603069f45459")
	)
	(text "U6  A8-A15"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 143.89 49.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f6275a78-67cb-4295-a222-f9df2f683984")
	)
	(text "U11  data out, to DO0-DO7"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 143.89 137.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fa57d4ad-6cf9-4a82-a325-12e62462eadb")
	)
	(text "Open-collector translators: five SN74LVC07AN hex buffers, 14-pin dual in-line, powered from 3.3 V. A low from the FPGA pulls the bus line down. When the FPGA lets go, the input pull-up turns that output off. The spare input on the last buffer is tied to 3.3 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.05 228.35 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ffd86bd9-b0eb-465c-bf8f-99a85966f90c")
	)
